From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Anthony Fu (via agent)" <reg-github-bot@antfu.me>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 09:42:24 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat: name a project while adding it

Cloning vitejs/devtools and nuxt/devtools into the same parent folder
collides, because the clone folder is always the repository name. The Add
Project flow now has a name step: for a GitHub clone the name becomes the
clone folder (and so the project name), and for an existing folder it sets
the project's display name through the existing project rename RPC.

The clone request gains an optional directoryName, validated as a single
path segment, and the daemon advertises it as
server_info.features.projectGithubCloneDirectoryName. Clients that omit
the field clone into the repository name as before, and the app only shows
the clone name step on hosts that advertise the flag.

Fork-Change: F-6
